# Build context for all three Dockerfiles is the repository root. Only
# patches/ and runtime/ (Dockerfile, Dockerfile-Ollama) and training/
# (Dockerfile-ComfyUI) are COPYed from it; Dockerfile-ComfyUI takes tools/
# through its own named build context. Everything else is documentation,
# host-side tooling, git metadata, or user data that would otherwise be hashed
# and shipped to the daemon on every build. The patterns below match the top
# level only, so the Python files under training/ and runtime/ are kept.
#
# This does not affect layer caching: BuildKit keys a COPY on the checksums of
# the files it actually copies, not on the whole context.
.git/
*.md
*.py
*.log
docs/
tools/
ollama-tools/
# Bytecode from running training/'s scripts on the host; the image compiles
# its own.
**/__pycache__
# Models, datasets, run output, caches, MIOpen databases and local
# environments: hundreds of GB.
ComfyUI/
workspace/
ollama/
miopen/
setup-logs/
.venv/
